Yes, because the monsters aren't there. But it requires *less* skill than
nethack does by itself, leading you to a false sense of security to the
point of save scumming becoming a crutch or addiction if you like. Once
you've done it, switching back to nethack without save scumming is very
hard. I know, I did it to learn the first 20 levels back a few years ago.
Not your method (in linux or *nix, specifically bash. Ubuntu is just the
company that put the free software together on a disk. I hope you didn't
pay more than $10-15 per disk for it. There's a contract about how much
can be charged) I just copied the files to another directory and then back
once I died and did a recover. You loose the time on the level you die on,
but everything else is there. I was paranoid of what I would run into,
because I ran into Ludios (scared the s*it out of me that time - died of
course), the castle for the tune - same as above, and then a Minotaur
above that a couple of times. Not good. Couldn't get my armor/weapons
figured out to stay good. Eventually, once I figured that out I got as far
as dying on the run to level 1. Now I'm playing spork actually. Think
nethack is hard? Try running into a Minotaur at mines end. Three times
out of 5 times I've been there. Not a chameleon either. I checked last
time. Two of my top five scores have "killed by a Minotaur". 

Really, use it to learn what you're likely to see in the main dungeon
below sokoban, and what kind of weapons/armor you'll need, but anything
else and you'll be spending weeks going nowhere. It took me about 4 weeks
of play to get to the vibrating square the first time. It takes about 4
hours to do the mines and sokoban. And that's a bit slow. I like to get
everything that early. So I completely explore the mines and check all
non-cursed armor. 

Besides, it *is* cheating. Has been since disk drives were invented. I
know people that used to do it with Civilization - you got a gain out of
it if you did it right. 

Or better yet don't do it at all and then you won't have to quit.


